From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:21:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix(ui): a toast no longer blocks the Enter and Escape
 hotkeys

Every toast is an alertdialog (react-aria's useToast), so the open-overlay
guard of useHotkey took any toast on screen for an open dialog: since Enter
was added to the guard, the "snapshot saved" toast (8 s; errors 10 s) kept
Enter from starting or accepting an episode, and Escape from discarding one
already before.

Only what is modal counts now: a dialog or alertdialog unless it is
aria-modal="false", and a menu or listbox; nothing in react-aria's toast
region counts. Tested with a real ToastContainer: Enter and Escape fire with a
toast on screen, also right after a capture's toast, and stay with a real
modal dialog (also with a toast on screen), an open menu and the open recent
snapshots list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
